## Story Description
Document the three new rule types, the per-engagement config override mechanism, and the unit price fields in CLAUDE.md. Future sessions need this to understand why _apply_engagement_overrides() exists, what the new rules fire on, and the column_mapping limitation for unit_price.

## Acceptance Criteria
- Edit file: CLAUDE.md — in the 'Rule types implemented' table under Phase 6, add three new rows: SPEND_CONCENTRATION_RISK (top supplier > concentration_threshold_pct of multi-supplier L2 category), EARLY_PAYMENT_DISCOUNT_CAPTURE (suppliers with has_early_payment_discount=1; captures contractually available discounts), BEST_PRICE_EXTRAPOLATION (benchmarks unit_price across suppliers in same L3 category; no-ops when unit_price absent)
- Edit file: CLAUDE.md — add new subsection '### Per-Engagement Recommendation Config' under Phase 6 documenting: overrides stored in engagements.recommendation_config_json as JSON; GET/PATCH /recommendations/config endpoints in recommendations router; RecommendationEngine accepts engagement_id param; _apply_engagement_overrides() uses setattr on config.recommendations; new RecommendationsConfig fields: concentration_threshold_pct (default 0.80), min_discount_opportunity (default 1000.0), min_price_benchmark_transactions (default 5); frontend settings panel on RecommendationsPage
- Edit file: CLAUDE.md — add note about unit_price: unit_price (Float) and unit_of_measure (Text) added as nullable columns to transactions table and CanonicalTransaction; BEST_PRICE_EXTRAPOLATION rule no-ops when absent; note the column_mapping bug: frontend UploadPage sends column_mapping but ingest_to_raw() does not use it — unit_price only populates if CSV column is already named unit_price

